<title>AUSTRALIA: Biggest gains/falls for ASX 100 index in past year.</title>
<headline>Biggest gains/falls for ASX 100 index in past year.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a list of the 10 largest gaining and falling stocks for Australian companies included in the Australian Stock Exchange's ASX 100 index for the year to July 25.</p>
<p>Top 10 largest gains in year</p>
<p>						 Percent</p>
<p>Rank Name			 Price     change</p>
<p> 1   Oil Search		  3.87     204.72</p>
<p> 2   Sthn Pac Pete	     3.80	74.31</p>
<p> 3   A N Z Bank		 10.48	74.09</p>
<p> 4   Transurban Group     1060.00	73.49</p>
<p> 5   Howard Smith	     13.62	72.41</p>
<p> 6   Hardie Inds		 4.40	71.21</p>
<p> 7   Natl Aust Bank	   19.28	64.09</p>
<p> 8   Fletcher-Energy div     4.43	62.42</p>
<p> 9   Aust Gas Light	    8.41	58.98</p>
<p>10   FLC-Building div	  3.83	58.77</p>
<p>Top 10 largest falls in year</p>
<p>						 Percent</p>
<p>Rank Name			 Price     change</p>
<p> 1   Acacia Resources	  1.40     -53.33</p>
<p> 2   Goldfields		  1.40     -51.72</p>
<p> 3   Newcrest Mining	   2.61     -48.80</p>
<p> 4   Sons Of Gwalia	    4.70     -47.83</p>
<p> 5   Plutonic Rsc		3.59     -44.77</p>
<p> 6   Davids Limited	    1.11     -39.34</p>
<p> 7   RGC			   3.97     -35.45</p>
<p> 8   Great Central	     2.49     -28.45</p>
<p> 9   Normandy Min		1.48     -26.37</p>
<p>10   Crown			 2.09     -25.39</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
